BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Eight Step Recovery Group For Men
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20260305T170000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20260305T183000
UID:3d574cdb495893dd1d5e16ea@lbc-ics
DESCRIPTION:Eight Step Recovery is an alternative recovery program to the 
 12-Step program of Alcoholic Anonymous. The program is a set of mindfulnes
 s teachings outlining a suggested course of action for recovery from addic
 tion\, stinking thinking\, negative mental states\, and compulsive and obs
 essive behaviours.
URL:https://www.londonbuddhistcentre.com/whats-on/eight-step-recovery-for-
 men-5-mar
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Men's Intensive Long Weekend
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20260305T190000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20260305T150000
UID:1dfb4f2541ac477955d3d6d2@lbc-ics
DESCRIPTION:Jnanavaca and Maitreyabandhu have been creating these signific
 ant retreats for a few years now. They have a strong dharmic vision: a vig
 orous exploration of deep dharma principles\, coupled with intensive medit
 ation input and a strongly devotional approach.
URL:https://www.londonbuddhistcentre.com/whats-on/mens-intensive-long-week
 end-2026
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Thursday Night Class: Meditation & In-Conversation
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20260305T191500
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20260305T211500
UID:940b212adef91a245d382cbb@lbc-ics
DESCRIPTION:These pith teachings - such as 'reduce input' and 'don't accep
 t yourself' - were given to members of our Buddhist Order by its founder\,
  Bhante Urgyen Sangharakshita. We will continue to celebrate Bhante's life
  and legacy by exploring these teachings during the centenary of his birth
 .
URL:https://www.londonbuddhistcentre.com/whats-on/thurs-night-5-mar
END:VEVENT
